 2. 💸 Musk merger math 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep . (SpaceX shares began publicly trading on June 12.) Chart: Dan Primack/Axios The potential SpaceX-Tesla merger took an orbital leap forward yesterday, with Elon Musk calling it "a good idea" and both companies forming special committees to discuss a deal, Axios' Dan Primack reports. 

 Such a deal would be the largest corporate tie-up in history. 📈 By the numbers: SpaceX ended the day yesterday with a $1.95 trillion market cap, making it the country's seventh most valuable company.

 Tesla landed in 11th place with a $1.48 trillion market cap. Shares of both companies are up sharply today. The bottom line: Musk cautioned that saying a merger will definitely happen is "overstating it," but he tends to move very fast once he gets the transactional truck rolling.

