 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Chiricahua National Park. Photo: Ron Kerbo/National Park Service via AP 🥾 Southeastern Arizona's Chiricahua (cheery-cow-uh) is officially the country's first new national park in six years. Interior Secretary Doug Burgum said : "Chiricahua's towering rock spires, rich Apache heritage and remarkable biodiversity make it one of America's most extraordinary landscapes." Go deeper . 🇮🇱 Democratic congressional nominee Brad Lander of New York was among about 80 activists detained by Israeli security forces today in the West Bank. Lander, who said he was later released, wrote on X : "We were simply harvesting olives in a grove near Nehalim in the West Bank. The occupation is a crime under international law. Harvesting olives isn't a crime under any law I know." Go deeper . 🗳️ Cook Political Report shifted Minnesota's Senate race from "Likely Democrat" to "Lean Democrat," showing the contest between Lt. Gov. Peggy Flanagan (D) and former NFL broadcaster Michele Tafoya (R) is tighter than expected. Go deeper . 🎤 "SNL" star Kenan Thompson said he would have a candid conversation with Shane Gillis if he returned to host after Gillis' controversial monologue. "I don't know him to be a mean person necessarily," Thompson said at the Axios Media Trends Live event in Manhattan yesterday. "But yeah, if he were to come back, I'm sure we would have a conversation of, like: 'How do you think that went?'" Go deeper . 
 
