 4. ☄️ 1 for the road: Meteor shower alert 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Orionids meteor shower seen from Daqing City, China, in 2020. Photo: Costfoto/Future Publishing via Getty Images The Orionids meteor shower — one of the best of the year — peaks overnight tonight.

 The annual shower comes as dust left by comet 1P/Halley burns up in Earth's atmosphere. 🔭 With dark enough skies, stargazers can expect to see at least 10–20 meteors an hour.

 The Orionids are known for especially bright, streaky fireballs. Viewing tips . 

 
 
